{"pageid":4265,"title":"Burls","displaytitle":"<span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Burls</span>","revid":21987,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Burls</b> are a unique sub-resource to trees<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"autonumber\" href=\"https://oaklands.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Trees\">[1]</a>. Unlike trees, however, burls are unique in that their wood cannot be turned into <i>refined planks</i>, but are instead highly valued by players for their unique sanded/<i>plank</i> texture. Burls also cannot be chopped into smaller pieces. \n</p><p>Burls can rarely spawn on the largest of specific living trees identified by the fact they also spawn dead variants such as stumps and fallen logs. \n</p><p>As of writing the examples currently include: Oak, Petrified Oak, Birch, Red Birch, Pine, Blue Pine, Red Maple, Olive, Willow, Sakura, Acacia, Sequoia, and Spruce.\n</p><p>And now Shadow since the introduction of the <i>secret update</i>.\n</p><p>One unique case among burls is the <a href=\"/wiki/Beehive\" title=\"Beehive\">Beehive</a>, which is considered a woodburl material by the game but can grow on multiple species of tree leaves and may also be put through the <a href=\"/wiki/Press_Machine\" title=\"Press Machine\">Press Machine</a> after being planked in order to make a jar of <b>Honey</b>.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"thumb mw-halign-center show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Frame\" style=\"width: 942px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/3/37/Pine_and_sequoia_burls.png/revision/latest?cb=20250727140633\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"A pine and sequoia burl.\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/oaklands/images/3/37/Pine_and_sequoia_burls.png/revision/latest?cb=20250727140633\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"942\" height=\"549\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Pine and sequoia burls.png\" data-image-key=\"Pine_and_sequoia_burls.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a> \t \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Pine_and_sequoia_burls.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p class=\"caption\">A pine and sequoia burl.</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<p><br />\nAll tree Burl types:\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Oak_Burl\" title=\"Oak Burl\">Oak Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Petrified_Oak_Burl\" title=\"Petrified Oak Burl\">Petrified Oak Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Birch_Burl\" title=\"Birch Burl\">Birch Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Red_Birch_Burl\" title=\"Red Birch Burl\">Red Birch Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Pine_Burl\" title=\"Pine Burl\">Pine Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Blue_Pine_Burl\" title=\"Blue Pine Burl\">Blue Pine Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Red_Maple_Burl\" title=\"Red Maple Burl\">Red Maple Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Olive_Burl\" title=\"Olive Burl\">Olive Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Willow_Burl\" title=\"Willow Burl\">Willow Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Sakura_Burl\" title=\"Sakura Burl\">Sakura Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Acacia_Burl\" title=\"Acacia Burl\">Acacia Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Sequoia_Burl\" title=\"Sequoia Burl\">Sequoia Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Spruce_Burl\" title=\"Spruce Burl\">Spruce Burl</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Shadow_tree_burl\" title=\"Shadow tree burl\">Shadow tree burl</a></li></ul>\n<p><s>There's rumors of a burl for the <a href=\"/wiki/Suiratcal\" title=\"Suiratcal\">Suiratcal</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Heavenly_Tree\" title=\"Heavenly Tree\">Heavenly Tree</a> however they are likely so rare that they are just rumors.</s>\nThis cannot be correct. Burls only spawn on trees that also spawn a dead version such as stumps and fallen logs - unlike Suiratcal and Heavenly.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260903163052\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.018 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 1/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.9_prod_oaklands:pcache:idhash:4265-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timestamp 20260903163052 and revision id 21987. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>","categories":[],"links":[{"title":"Acacia Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Beehive","exists":true},{"title":"Birch Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Blue Pine Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Heavenly Tree","exists":true},{"title":"Oak Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Olive Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Petrified Oak Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Pine Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Press Machine","exists":true},{"title":"Red Birch Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Red Maple Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Sakura Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Sequoia Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Shadow tree burl","exists":true},{"title":"Spruce Burl","exists":true},{"title":"Suiratcal","exists":true},{"title":"Willow Burl","exists":true}],"images":["Pine_and_sequoia_burls.png"]}
